+# Defensive audit sweep: ping-api, 2026-10-03
+
+## Context
+Scope: the unauthenticated ping endpoints and the API-key gate: `hc/api/views.py` (`ping`,
+`ping_by_slug`), `hc/api/decorators.py`, `hc/api/urls.py`. Trigger: first sweep on this zone;
+the registry had no row for it. No changes in the zone since the pinned upstream commit.
+
+## Delegation
+One reviewer in a fresh session, with the brief from the skill. Pre-read: `README.md`,
+`SECURITY.md`, `docs/audits/categories.md`. No previous reports existed; the registry was
+bootstrapped in this run.
+
+## Verification
+| Finding | Zone | Verdict | Claimed | Verified | Reservations | Proof |
+|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
+| PING-1 `/ping/<uuid>` accepts unauthenticated requests and stores the body | ping-api | FALSE POSITIVE | High | - | by design: the check code is the capability; malformed and unknown codes answer 404 | existing `hc/api/tests/test_ping.py::PingTestCase::test_it_handles_bad_uuid` |
+| PING-2 ping body stored without a size bound | ping-api | FALSE POSITIVE | Medium | - | `request.body` is sliced to `PING_BODY_LIMIT` before storage | existing `hc/api/tests/test_ping.py::PingTestCase::test_it_chops_long_body` |
+
+## Confirmed defects
+None.
+
+## Refused or unconfirmed candidates
+- PING-1, FALSE POSITIVE (lens: claim correctness). The product contract is that whoever holds a
+  check's code can ping it; there is no user to authenticate. The code is a UUID the server
+  generates (`hc/api/models.py:196`, `default=uuid.uuid4`, not editable), an unknown code answers
+  404 (`hc/api/views.py:188` to `hc/api/views.py:192`), and a malformed one is rejected by the URL
+  converter. Accepted by the owner as a product rule, so this item is closed, not pending.
+- PING-2, FALSE POSITIVE (lens: existing mitigation). `hc/api/views.py:211` truncates the body to
+  `settings.PING_BODY_LIMIT` (`hc/settings.py:272`, default 10000 bytes) and the response
+  announces the limit (`hc/api/views.py:241` to `hc/api/views.py:242`). An operator who sets the
+  limit to `None` opts out knowingly; `test_it_allows_unlimited_body` documents that choice.
+
+## Coverage
+Read: `hc/api/views.py` lines 170 to 290, `hc/api/decorators.py`, `hc/api/urls.py`,
+`hc/api/tests/test_ping.py`. Skipped: the authenticated management API (`checks`, `channels`,
+`badges`, `metrics`) and the integrations under `hc/api/transports.py`, each a zone of its own.
+Lenses applied: exploitability, claim correctness, existing mitigation.
