+# Audit categories
+
+Categories, not patterns. A new pattern lands under an existing category. "Covered by" names the
+control in this project; the last column says whether a test asserts it.
+
+| Category | Covered by | Enforced mechanically? |
+|---|---|---|
+| API authentication | `authorize` and `authorize_read` in `hc/api/decorators.py`: `X-Api-Key` header, read-only keys flagged on the request | yes: `hc/api/tests/` |
+| Ownership per project | views compare `check.project_id` with `request.project.id` and answer 403 (for example `hc/api/views.py:483`) | yes: `hc/api/tests/` |
+| Capability URLs | check codes are server-generated UUIDs (`hc/api/models.py:196`); unknown codes answer 404 | yes: `hc/api/tests/test_ping.py` |
+| Request size limits | `PING_BODY_LIMIT` applied in `hc/api/views.py:211` | yes: `test_it_chops_long_body` |
+| CSRF | API views are `csrf_exempt` by design; browser views rely on the Django middleware | partly |
